cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Winter chill projections for apricot in Spain: 'Búlida' and its low-chill somatic mutant
  'Búlida Precoz' over cultivable land, 1976-2100
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Daniel
    family-names: González-Palazón
    affiliation: Estación Experimental de Aula Dei (EEAD-CSIC), Zaragoza, Spain
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0001-2810-9468'
  - given-names: José A.
    family-names: Egea
    affiliation: Centro de Edafología y Biología Aplicada del Segura (CEBAS-CSIC), Murcia, Spain
    # orcid: pending, to be added once confirmed with the co-author
repository-code: 'https://github.com/DanielGP121/plinius-apricot-winter-chill'
abstract: >-
  Code for an agroclimatic analysis of winter chill accumulation in Spain, computed with the
  Dynamic Model under the Fishman et al. (1987) parametrisation. It combines the PNACC AR6 climate
  projections regionalised to weather stations, two observational products spliced into a record
  running from 1976 to 2025, and CORINE Land Cover, in order to map where the apricot cultivar
  'Búlida' stops meeting its chill requirement while its somatic mutant 'Búlida Precoz' still meets
  its own, expressed as area of cultivable land rather than as a count of stations.
keywords:
  - winter chill
  - dormancy
  - Prunus armeniaca
  - climate change adaptation
  - chill portions
  - dynamic model
  - CMIP6
  - Spain
